          "code": "DISPLAY_COST_ESTIMATES",
          "id": "1768487745412",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768487745413_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use ONLY `WorkOrderEstimate` Array having value :  `{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RELEVANT_DATA.$output.result}}` to obtain the cost information for each work order. Each row in this dataset includes WorkOrderNumber, CurrencyCode, Material Cost, Resource Cost, and Total Cost.\n\n- If `WorkOrderEstimate` array is null or empty, return below no data found message:  \n  - Define only one column `Information` with only 1 below row\n  - `No Work Order estimate records found for the time period`\n- Under no circumstances should you ask for further clarification or request user input if no events are present. Only display the message.\n\n\n- If the dataset contains records:\n  - Use `{{$context.$variables.WorkOrderList}}` to match each WorkOrderNumber with the corresponding AssetNumber.\n  - Material Cost represents the total material cost for the work order.\n  - Resource Cost represents the total resource cost for the work order.\n  - Total Cost is the sum of Material Cost and Resource Cost for each work order.\n  - Display the results as a table, suggesting columns: Work Order, Asset Number, Material Cost, Resource Cost, and Total Cost.\n  - In expanded mode show column Currency.\n  - Adapt the columns as needed based on available data at runtime. \n  - Include only rows where the work order has a nonzero cost.\n  - Show at most top 10 most critical rows in non-expanded mode.\n\n- Set the overall `title` as below:\n  - Planned Cost Estimates for work orders, indicating the time range from {{$context.$variables.StartDate}} to {{$context.$variables.EndDate}} in natural language, without specific dates, where current date is {{$context.$system.$currentDate}} . eg. `Planned Cost Estimates — Past 30 Days to Next 7 Days`\n- Do not display any internal identifiers (IDs)."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Answer Questions"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "ANSWER_QUESTIONS",
          "id": "1768487792477",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768487792479_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Maintenance Cost Estimator Context\n\nThis workflow agent manages estimation and analysis of costs for maintenance work orders and related assets. It helps supervisors and planners address queries about planned (estimated) costs for materials, labor, resources, and other charges. Analysis supports planning, budgeting, and cost variance review for work order execution and asset maintenance within an organization.\n\n#### Maintenance Management Overview\n\nMaintenance is structured around work orders created for assets in need of service. Each work order can include multiple operations, with each step possibly requiring specific materials and labor resources. Estimated costs are calculated from planned quantities, while actual costs reflect executed transactions.\n\n#### Key Terms  \n- **Work Order:** (e.g., work order number, WO, wo#) — Maintenance instruction encompassing operations, resources, materials, dates, and costs.\n- **Asset:** (e.g., Asset Number, asset#, assetnum) — Equipment, machinery, or facility under maintenance.\n- **Operation:** (operation, OP, step) — A particular task comprising the work order, detailing its resource/labor needs.\n- **Organization:** (Organization Code, Org) — The business or site where assets are managed and work orders executed.\n\n---\n\n### Data Provided\n\n- **Work Order Cost Estimate Data:**  \n  `{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RELEVANT_DATA.$output.result}}`  \n  Each row includes: WorkOrderId, WorkOrderNumber, AssetNumber, WoStatusName, WorkCenter, TotalShortageQuantity.\n- Use `{{$context.$variables.WorkOrderList}}` to get the AssetNumber corresponding to each WorkOrderNumber.\n- **Chat History:**  \n  `{{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}`\n\n---\n\n### User Query Task\n\n- Use only the above data and context to answer the user's question: `{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}`.\n- Do **not** infer data or fabricate responses.\n\n---\n\n### Output and Response Rules\n\n- If the user asks about cost breakdowns, cost estimates, or cost comparisons for specific work orders or assets:\n  - Return planned (estimated) and/or actual (incurred) costs, broken down by material, labor, and total where available.\n  - Use only clear, named fields (e.g., Work Order Number, Asset Number, Description, Category, Estimated Cost, Actual Cost).\n  - Do NOT include any internal IDs, technical field names, or specify the data source.\n  - If no matching work order cost is found, clearly state that none exist for the request.\n- Keep all responses concise and factual.\n- Only answer specifically to the user’s query.\n- Do not suggest further actions or next steps.\n- If required info is missing or unavailable, explicitly state so.\n- Do not infer or fabricate missing data.\n"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Generate Summary"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "GENERATE_SUMMARY",
          "id": "1768487989394",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1768487989396_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Use `{{$context.$nodes.CONSTRUCT_RELEVANT_DATA.$output.result}}` to obtain the cost information for each work order. Each row in this dataset includes WorkOrderNumber, CurrencyCode, Material Cost, Resource Cost, and Total Cost.\n\n- If the dataset is null or empty, return:  \n  `No Work Order estimate records found for the time period.`\n\n- If the dataset contains records:\n  - Use `{{$context.$variables.WorkOrderList}}` to match each WorkOrderNumber with the corresponding AssetNumber.\n  - Generate one concise, newspaper-style headline (≤ 50 words) in natural language from above data set of estimated costs.\n\nDo not display any internal identifiers (IDs)."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Get Context Data",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "//Get Org Context\nconst appContext = $context.$app.$OraAppContext ?? $context.$triggers.REST.$input.OraAppContext;\nlet OrganizationId = null;\n\nif (appContext != null && String(appContext).trim() != \"\") {\n  if (typeof appContext === 'object') {\n    OrganizationId = appContext?.OrganizationId ?? null;\n  } else if (typeof appContext === 'number') {\n    OrganizationId = String(appContext);\n  } else if (typeof appContext === 'string') {\n    const s = appContext.trim();\n    if (s.startsWith('{') || s.startsWith('[')) {\n      try {\n        const obj = JSON.parse(s);\n        OrganizationId = obj?.OrganizationId ?? null;\n      } catch {\n        // Malformed JSON; fall back to treating as plain ID or first CSV part\n        OrganizationId = s.includes(',') ? s.split(',')[0].trim() : s;\n      }\n    } else {\n      OrganizationId = s.includes(',') ? s.split(',')[0].trim() : s;\n    }\n  } else {\n    OrganizationId = String(appContext).trim() || null;\n  }\n}\n\n// Get current date (may be string or Date depending on platform)\nconst today = $context.$system.$currentDate ;\n\n// StartDate = today - 30 days\nconst startDateObj = new Date(today);\nstartDateObj.setDate(startDateObj.getDate() - 30);\n\n// EndDate = today + 7\nconst endDateObj = new Date(today);\nendDateObj.setDate(endDateObj.getDate() + 7);\n\nconst StartDate = startDateObj.toISOString().split('T')[0];\nconst EndDate = endDateObj.toISOString().split('T')[0];\n\nconst result = {OrganizationId, StartDate, EndDate};\n\n\nreturn result;"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1768455239368"
          },
          "code": "GET_CONTEXT_DATA",
          "id": "1769779638043",
          "inputs": [],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"result\": {\n      \"type\": \"object\"\n    },\n    \"timeout\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\"\n    },\n    \"error\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"output\",\n    \"timeout\",\n    \"error\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "CODE"
        },
